your loader data might be out of date or stale. For example, if you have a route that displays a list of posts, and you have a loader function that fetches the list of posts from an API, you might want to invalidate the route matches for that route any time a new post is created so that the list of posts is always up-to-date."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":" is not supplied, all committed, cached, and in-flight match generations are invalidated."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"filter"},{"type":"text","value":" is supplied, it is evaluated against committed, cached, and in-flight matches. Selecting one generation invalidates every committed, cached, or in-flight generation with the same match ID."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalidation reruns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":"; reusable loader data is marked stale and reloads through the normal loading protocol. Route-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" remains reusable while the match ID is unchanged."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sync"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", stale loader work is blocking and the returned promise resolves after it finishes instead of leaving a background refresh detached."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forcePending"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", selected routes that need loading enter the normal pending protocol